    },
    {
      "text": "In a medium saucepan, over medium to high heat, bring beer to a boil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GHtfFscbEeBtHDEzEhyLQF7lEJY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-recipe-21333-lobster-tails-steamed-in-beer-step-02-123a7ca51b3d42b7bdde27789cd652db.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21333/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "If lobster tails are still in the shell, split the shell lengthwise first.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tiiEXLqq5Si5xGs-OsyVNRP-9jA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-recipe-21333-lobster-tails-steamed-in-beer-step-03-f451bc9d0ca44250b0e5203826d550a1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/21333/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place a steamer basket on top of the saucepan; place thawed lobster tails in the basket and cover. Reduce heat and simmer for 8 minutes.",
